      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5d7322991ba4827d4243fb75",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Add on to that, the fact (I've noticed lately) that half the time, it won't even let you type in the password via keyboard when you're running in VR. (Don't know why it's failing, the other half of the time it works fine.  In all cases I've had it happen, the VRC window has focus, so that's not it.)\n\nNot to mention when you need to put in a TOTP, you have to get the TOTP, go back to VR, put it in, and hope you do all that before the TOTP expires in 30 seconds.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-09-07T03:23:05.812Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While I know there's the copy-paste method, it's very frustrating to try and click the screen with the controller, and then (without hitting any other buttons on controller) to CTRL+P the password in on only the password field not the username field.\n\nIf the login screen was the same for desktop and for headset user (do the dual screen mode like with Stream Camera), it would be tremendously easier to login when the credentials expire.\n\nMy alternative right now is to always start up in Desktop mode, check for login expiration, login, restart the game in VR mode, and continue on.\n\nI also don't want to have to memorize my randomized password, nor make it easier to bruteforce.",
